# Applying worktree changes to main branch

**Do not use** Cursor’s “Apply worktree to current branch” — it incorrectly writes to `/tilemap` (root path) and fails with `EROFS: read-only file system`.

Use one of these instead:

1. **Patch (from worktree):**
   ```bash
   cd /Users/jaceksroga/.cursor/worktrees/tilemap/<worktree-name>
   git diff main -- <files> > /tmp/changes.patch
   cd /Users/jaceksroga/tilemap
   git apply /tmp/changes.patch
   ```

2. **Copy files:**  
   `cp` from the worktree path (e.g. `.../worktrees/tilemap/jpi/src/...`) to `/Users/jaceksroga/tilemap/...`.

3. **Merge/cherry-pick:**  
   If changes are committed in the worktree branch, from main: `git merge <branch>` or `git cherry-pick <commit>`.
